# Line endings: the repository stores text files with LF, and they are checked out with LF on
# every platform, regardless of the clone's `core.autocrlf` setting (Git for Windows defaults it to
# `true` system-wide, which used to give CRLF working copies that the `mixed-line-ending --fix=lf`
# pre-commit hook then kept "fixing" even though the committed content was already LF).
# `text=auto` lets Git leave files it detects as binary alone; the explicit entries below don't
# rely on that detection.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files need CRLF to run reliably under cmd.exe.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Byte-exact content: never convert line endings (see the matching `exclude` in .pre-commit-config.yaml).
#   - test fixtures and "truth" files that tests compare verbatim;
#   - R script templates echoed verbatim into generated scripts, compared against truth files;
#   - vendored third-party report assets.
tests/test_files/** -text
rnalysis/data_files/r_templates/** -text
rnalysis/data_files/report_templates/** -text

# Binaries
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
